      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "Label": "Introduction",
          "content": "The relationship between obesity or overweight and pulmonary functions has not been investigated in Sri Lankan children previously. Therefore, we aimed to study the effects of obesity/overweight on dynamic lung functions in healthy school children in Sri Lanka."
        },
        {"Label": "Methods"},
        {
          "Label": "Results",
          "content": "Of 275 children 55 (20%) were \u2018obese/ overweight\u2019. BMI has no significant relationship to any of the pulmonary function parameters. However, in contrast to what is expected, mean values of FVC, FEV1 and FEF 25-75% were lower in \u2018normal weight\u2019 group (Table 2)."
        },
        {
          "Label": "Conclusions",
          "content": "No significant difference was detected in spirometry parameters between obese/overweight and normal weight school children in our study."
        }
      ]},
